{"name":"Squirt","hex":"#95bcc5","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"squirt","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An instrument from which a liquid is forcefully ejected in a small, quick stream.","A small, quick stream; a jet."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be thrown out, or ejected, in a rapid stream, from a narrow orifice.","To cause to be ejected, in a rapid stream, from a narrow orifice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/squirt"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ascidiacea","blocks":[{"text":"Ascidiacea, commonly known as the ascidians or sea squirts, is a paraphyletic class in the subphylum Tunicata of sac-like marine invertebrate filter feeders. Ascidians are characterized by a tough outer test or \"tunic\" made of the polysaccharide cellulose."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Cionaintestinalis.jpg/330px-Cionaintestinalis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ascidiacea","wikidata":"Q190090"},{"title":"Squirt (drink)","blocks":[{"text":"Squirt is a caffeine-free, grapefruit-flavored, carbonated soft drink, created in 1938 in Phoenix, Arizona. The brand competed primarily with The Coca-Cola Company's Fresca."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/91/The_logo_of_Squirt%2C_a_grapefruit_flavored_soda.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Squirt_(drink)","wikidata":"Q7582349"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Cionaintestinalis.jpg/500px-Cionaintestinalis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Cionaintestinalis.jpg/1280px-Cionaintestinalis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Cion